================================================================================
 NOTES (design decisions)
================================================================================
- Manifest marks the page "no API data sources — renders from navigation values /
  local state". The @Observable ApiLogsPageModel binds through an injected
  ApiLogsDataSource (Sendable, async load()/refresh()); the default Unavailable source
  yields a real empty state (never a fake row, ADR-011), a JSON-decoding source bridges
  the shared AdminStore.apiLogs/apiLogStats feeds (networking stays in the KMP core,
  P4 rule #3), and a Preview source drives all four states in previews + tests.
- HIG-native + adaptive (ADR-002): one scrolling column reflowing via adaptive grids;
  materials/tokens only (Color.TS/Font.TS/TSSpacing/TSRadius), shared components only
  (TSGlassPanel/TSStatCard/TSBadge/TSButton/TSSelect/TSTextField/TSEmptyState/
  TSErrorDisplay/TSAlertBanner/TSSpinner/TSCode/TSFadeIn). No web cloning, no inline
  hardcoded colours/typography, no raw HTML analogue.
- The web header RangePicker is not among the 9 enumerated panels and has no authorized
  string in the 30-key set; reproducing it would require either hardcoded literals or
  un-authorized keys, so it is out of the binding contract for this unit.

